two weeks to go until the cop 26 u.n  climate summit in glasgow it's been  described as the world's last best hope  to limit global warming but there may be  a big problem looming  when we spoke to u.s special envoy on  climate change john kerry earlier this  month he commented on the stalling  progress of a bill that contains a  sweeping plan to decarbonize america's  electricity the sausage making is not  pretty  but in the end they're going to have a  sausage i believe  but that is now in doubt because of this  man senator joe manchin a democrat from  the coal reliant state of west virginia  who wields a decisive vote in the senate  he is refusing to support the clean  power plan and it may be withdrawn  suddenly the united states a global  leader in the fight against climate  change urging other nations to do more  looks like it can't follow its own  advice with potentially huge  consequences  it makes it more difficult for the us to  push china and other countries to do  more  towards net zero emission reduction  targets in mid-century if china and  those other countries can say  you've set a target but you're not  making progress towards implementing it  which they've already put out as a  defensive shield against the pressure on  them to do more  america's domestic political problems  are not the only issue the government's  cop 26 unit in westminster is having to  consider at the moment  it's emerged that some of the summit's  main corporate sponsors including skye  have previously written to the  government raising concerns about the  way it was being organized and activists  are complaining about ongoing problems  with the availability and cost of  accommodation which might prevent them  from attending  in a statement a cop 26 spokesperson  said we are committed to hosting an  inclusive summit in two weeks time which  showcases innovative work from a range  of businesses and civil society groups  who are committed to tackling climate  change together ministers are continuing  to focus their time on helping to secure  a positive outcome in glasgow  organizing an international summit is  not an easy task and at this crucial  moment as nearly 200 nations each with  individual needs and pressures prepare  to gather in glasgow delivering a  successful one will be even harder  hannah thomas peter sky news in  westminster
 

